9.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {{1,4},{2,5},{3}}

I am reading the Kō-zu as it is reproduced in the standard Genji incense diagrams, with the five vertical bars numbered 1–5 from left to right. In the plate for chapter 39 the two outer-left bars and the fourth bar are drawn with the same mark, so sticks 1 and 4 share a scent. The second and fifth bars are drawn with the matching mark, so sticks 2 and 5 share a scent. The third bar is drawn with a different mark and stands alone.

That gives the equivalence classes 1∼4, 2∼5 and 3 alone, i.e. in increasing order of the minima {{1,4}, {2,5}, {3}}.

