6.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The chapter-20 anchor fixes the indexing. Chapter 20 is given as {{1,3,4},{2},{5}} which in restricted growth notation is 1 2 1 1 3. In the ordinary 1-based lexicographic RGS list 1 2 1 1 3 is the 18th string, so ch = RGS rank +2, i.e. rank = ch-2. That is the convention used by the majority.

Hence ch 39 → rank = 39-2 = 37 in 1-based RGS order.

Counting RGS lexicographically:
a2=1 gives ranks 1-15;
a2=2,a3=1 gives 16-25;
a2=2,a3=2 gives 26-35;
a2=2,a3=3 starts at 36.
Rank 37 is the second string in the 1 2 3 block with a4=1, a5=2:
a = 1 2 3 1 2.
a1=1, a2=2, a3=3, a4=1, a5=2.
Blocks by equal a:
a=1 → {1,4}
a=2 → {2,5}
a=3 → {3}
In increasing-minimum order {{1,4},{2,5},{3}}.

This is the three-block two-pairs-plus-singleton pattern traditionally quoted for Takekawa/Miyuki, ch.39: sticks 1 and 4 share a scent, sticks 2 and 5 share a scent, stick 3 alone.

The 0-based / +1 shift confusion is visible in the discussion. With 0-based counting chapter n is the (n-2)-th 0-based RGS, i.e. the (n-1)-th 1-based RGS. That shift gives the next string 1 2 3 1 3 ↔ {{1,4},{2},{3,5}}, the 38th 1-based RGS often quoted in the literature as the “usual” chapter-39 pattern. Colleagues 10,15,18,20,3 explicitly note this off-by-one.

Alternative minority proposals appear in round 0: {{1,5},{2},{3,4}}, {{1,3},{2},{4,5}}, {{1,4},{2,3},{5}}, {{1,2,4,5},{3}}, {{1},{2,3},{4,5}} etc. These correspond to different enumerations / printings of the kō no zu and are not consistent with the chapter-20 anchor 1 2 1 1 3 ↔ {{1,3,4},{2},{5}}.

Current belief with the anchor fixed as in the prompt is {{1,4},{2,5},{3}} for chapter 39. If the 0-based convention is adopted the next RGS {{1,4},{2},{3,5}} is the commonly cited variant. Unresolved is which convention the question setter intends for the “vertical bars represent incense sticks numbered {1..5}” wording, but the anchor forces the 37th 1-based RGS.

